but it wasn't my fault.

735
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:32,084
I was needed across town.

736
00:45:32,200 --> 00:45:33,690
Still...

737
00:45:33,800 --> 00:45:35,131
made it.

738
00:45:35,240 --> 00:45:36,401
And...

739
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:38,568
this will be going out live, yes?

740
00:45:38,680 --> 00:45:41,650
Can you tell me,
who's interviewing me?

741
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:43,524
Yeah, it's, uh...

742
00:45:44,720 --> 00:45:46,404
Sod it!

743
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:56,122
I suppose a man like you
was always on his way.

744
00:45:56,240 --> 00:45:58,641
You met with PhiCorp today. Why?

745
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:01,525
You'll have to ask them.

746
00:46:01,640 --> 00:46:03,449
Did they mention
the name Jack Harkness?

747
00:46:03,560 --> 00:46:05,324
Have you heard that name?

748
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:07,925
Never.

749
00:46:08,040 --> 00:46:09,610
Why do you ask, Jack?

750
00:46:11,360 --> 00:46:15,365
I figured if you cared that much
about the name, it was probably yours.

751
00:46:20,520 --> 00:46:22,090
I just want you to talk.

752
00:46:22,200 --> 00:46:24,328
What about?

753
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:27,762
I saw you on television,
saying you feel forgiven

754
00:46:27,880 --> 00:46:29,166
for taking the life of a child.

755
00:46:29,280 --> 00:46:30,884
That's a lie.

756
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:32,809
I know that's a lie.

757
00:46:32,920 --> 00:46:35,810
How do you know that, Jack,

758
00:46:35,920 --> 00:46:37,684
- with such certainty?
- Tell the truth!

759
00:46:39,200 --> 00:46:41,043
The murder of Susie Cabina.

760
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:44,561
- You don't feel sorry at all.
- Oh...

761
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:47,848
The truth is,

762
00:46:47,960 --> 00:46:50,008
she flaunted it.

763
00:46:52,080 --> 00:46:53,241
Her innocence.

764
00:46:53,360 --> 00:46:56,409
Most people,
they get hit or whatever,

765
00:46:56,520 --> 00:46:58,841
it's hours

766
00:46:58,960 --> 00:47:01,042
before the bruises rise up,

767
00:47:01,160 --> 00:47:04,050
but they showed right away with her.

768
00:47:05,160 --> 00:47:07,322
And it was like...

769
00:47:07,440 --> 00:47:09,681
I was painting on her.

770
00:47:11,880 --> 00:47:13,370
And she looked so beautiful.

771
00:47:13,480 --> 00:47:15,244
I thought it couldn't get
any better than that.

772
00:47:15,360 --> 00:47:17,488
But, oh, Jack,

773
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:20,206
I swear to you,

774
00:47:20,320 --> 00:47:22,561
right then,

775
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:24,444
at the end,

776
00:47:24,560 --> 00:47:27,564
I felt her life leave, and...

777
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:30,081
and she left through me.

778
00:47:31,600 --> 00:47:33,045
Yeah!

779
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:35,971
You know that feeling?

780
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:40,084
I think you do.

781
00:47:40,200 --> 00:47:45,047
And I relive it every single night,
because...

782
00:47:45,160 --> 00:47:48,528
that was the best moment of my life.

783
00:47:54,480 --> 00:47:56,050
Now I understand.

784
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:00,128
You're doing all this
cos you're searching for one thing.

785
00:48:01,520 --> 00:48:04,569
One simple thing.

786
00:48:05,920 --> 00:48:07,649
Execution.

787
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:17,283
World without death,
so you get to live.

788
00:48:19,200 --> 00:48:20,565
And it's killing you.

789
00:48:23,440 --> 00:48:26,523
Jack, what are you going to do
with that recording?

790
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:29,564
We're in a broadcast centre.

791
00:48:29,680 --> 00:48:31,364
Figure I might broadcast it.

792
00:48:32,960 --> 00:48:35,247
Excellent idea.

793
00:48:35,360 --> 00:48:36,850
If only I didn't have to do this.

794
00:48:36,960 --> 00:48:39,008
Boys!

795
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:42,489
- Take that recording off him.
- Argh! Ah!

796
00:48:42,600 --> 00:48:46,446
I did visit PhiCorp, and they were
kind enough to offer me protection.

797
00:48:46,560 --> 00:48:48,085
In exchange for what?

798
00:48:49,600 --> 00:48:50,886
The message.

799
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:52,764
Don't hurt him.

800
00:48:52,880 --> 00:48:55,360
Just...get rid of him.

801
00:48:55,480 --> 00:48:58,086
It's nice to meet you, Jack Harkness.

802
00:48:58,200 --> 00:49:00,885
Well, you can hurt him a little,
but not the face.

803
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:04,049
That's how it's done these days.

804
00:49:04,160 --> 00:49:06,083
Let me be clear -

805
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:10,330
I'm not calling for free drugs
I'm calling for free access to drugs.

806
00:49:10,440 --> 00:49:12,408
I want every American
to have the power

807
00:49:12,520 --> 00:49:15,729
to be able to buy whatever they want
and need without a prescription.

808
00:49:15,840 --> 00:49:17,365
Ah!

809
00:49:17,480 --> 00:49:19,687
If that means that some drug companies
are gonna make a profit,

810
00:49:19,800 --> 00:49:23,486
then maybe that just ensures
that they'll take better care of us.

811
00:49:23,600 --> 00:49:24,806
Argh!

812
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:27,082
Because government has abandoned us.

813
00:49:27,200 --> 00:49:28,929
Argh! Ah!

814
00:49:29,040 --> 00:49:31,441
And I'm thinking
of companies like PhiCorp.

815
00:49:31,560 --> 00:49:33,403
Aargh! Ah! Ah!

816
00:49:33,520 --> 00:49:36,410
They'd never abandon us,
because they need us.

817
00:49:36,520 --> 00:49:38,443
Aargh! Ah!

818
00:49:38,560 --> 00:49:40,562
If we 're talking about medications,

819
00:49:40,680 --> 00:49:42,330
I have to say
that I'm some what of an expert'.

820
00:49:42,440 --> 00:49:44,363
I spent a lot of long years
in solitary confinement;

821
00:49:44,480 --> 00:49:49,008
dangerous man -
companies like PhiCorp tried to help.

822
00:49:49,120 --> 00:49:52,124
They put me on a drug reg/me

823
00:49:52,240 --> 00:49:54,561
- with every drug known in the world...
- Did you see him in there?

824
00:49:54,680 --> 00:49:55,966
Did you see Oswald Danes?

825
00:49:57,120 --> 00:49:59,600
- Did you touch him?
- Did I what?

826
00:49:59,720 --> 00:50:02,326
Oswald! Did you touch him?

827
00:50:02,440 --> 00:50:04,169
...they stick with us.

828
00:50:04,280 --> 00:50:08,968
And I'm asking you now
to join with me...

829
00:50:10,600 --> 00:50:12,409
...in this great enterprise

830
00:50:12,520 --> 00:50:17,287
as we all walk across the fragile skin
of this wide world...

831
00:50:17,400 --> 00:50:19,846
together.

832
00:50:19,960 --> 00:50:23,169
The future is now endless
and it's terrifying.

833
00:50:23,280 --> 00:50:26,170
I'm offering you my hand

834
00:50:26,280 --> 00:50:28,965
to walk on this long journey...

835
00:50:29,080 --> 00:50:30,605
together.

836
00:50:32,240 --> 00:50:33,844
Walk with me.

837
00:50:33,960 --> 00:50:35,724
That's all I ask.

838
00:50:37,360 --> 00:50:39,442
Walk with me.

839
00:50:40,560 --> 00:50:43,006
JACK: We need to find somewhere
to hide while we plan the assault'.

840
00:50:43,120 --> 00:50:46,761
Wow! Look at the horizon!
We've reached the edge of America.

841
00:50:46,880 --> 00:50:49,121
Hey, man. Believe.

842
00:50:50,080 --> 00:50:53,050
Let me ask you something.
What is this "dead is dead" shit?

843
00:50:53,160 --> 00:50:55,766
- Dead is dead.
- Dead is dead. That's me, huh?

844
00:50:55,880 --> 00:50:57,928
The moment I lose my platform,
I get thrown back to the mob.

845
00:50:58,040 --> 00:50:59,280
WOMAN: We are surrounded by people
who should have died.

846
00:50:59,400 --> 00:51:01,084
VERA: There's just nothing more
we could do for them.

847
00:51:01,200 --> 00:51:04,682
Segregation is vital and necessary.

848
00:51:04,800 --> 00:51:07,770
I have risen with unending life.

849
00:51:07,880 --> 00:51:10,486
These living deceased
should not have equal rights.

850
00:51:10,600 --> 00:51:12,170
You've compromised the security
of the entire mission.

851
00:51:12,280 --> 00:51:15,443
- They should be contained...
- I don't want to live forever.

852
00:51:15,560 --> 00:51:16,721
...and then they should wait...

853
00:51:16,840 --> 00:51:18,729
Torchwood keeps treating this
like it's a game.

854
00:51:18,840 --> 00:51:20,808
...because I believe
their passage to the afterlife

855
00:51:20,920 --> 00:51:22,081
has but paused

856
00:51:22,200 --> 00:51:25,363
- and when this miracle ends...
- I'm so tired.

857
00:51:25,480 --> 00:51:27,130
...Death will find them.

858
00:51:27,240 --> 00:51:29,447
Their time will come,
and they will die.
